      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "If the limiter store is down, fail open for reads, fail closed for expensive writes",
        "A limiter outage must never become a full API outage",
        "Decision is per endpoint class, stated before the incident, not during it"
      ],
      "title": "Fail-open vs fail-closed"
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "items": [
        "Usage events carry a unique request ID so retries never double-count",
        "Metering is asynchronous: it must never slow down or block the request path",
        "Billing reads the metered store, never the live counters"
      ],
      "title": "Metering accuracy"
    }
